  "summary": "C. Rajagopalachari argues that India should not accept the Colombo proposals concerning China merely in the name of Afro-Asian solidarity. He criticizes the Government's failure to state clearly what the proposals contain, whether India accepts them, and whether China has accepted them, noting that Parliament is expected to consider the matter while the Prime Minister's position remains uncertain.\n\nThe essay distinguishes genuine peace from solidarity used to preserve an anti-Western alignment. Rajagopalachari contends that China's aggression against India has already broken the basis for such solidarity and warns that accepting China's terms would reduce India to a satellite. He instead advocates resisting China with support from anti-communist Western powers while seeking peace and neighbourliness through mutual and balanced respect.",
